      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This is an interesting issue, on one hand, its a SSL warning, sounds scary, but like yt-dlp doesn't actually need to do anything here. When the yt-dlp process fails like this, the underlying video player just tries the same URL anyways. \n\nhttps://files.catbox.moe/ie49jp.mp4 is an upload of an animation called \"Polly Gone\" When I play it today, I get an error from the yt-dlp, but the video still plays. I wasn't able to specifically try uploading to litterbox, as it gave me an error today. \n\nBut yeah, asking the yt-dlp.exe that VRChat provides to do`yt-dlp.exe --no-cache-dir --rm-cache-dir -f \"(mp4/best)[height<=?480][height>=?64][width>=?64]\" --get-url https://files.catbox.moe/ie49jp.mp4` gets a nice error, but the video still plays in VRChat",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
